From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: validate ingress L3 flow identity

Bind router MACs and PPPoE physical/virtual ingress sessions with verified
transactions. QSDK detaches the physical port L3 binding on the first VLAN:
port L3 has priority over the VLAN VSI L3. Retaining it makes an
otherwise correctly installed tagged flow fail its source-interface check.
Share this transition across VLAN slots, reserve untagged fallback rules
outside bridge/tagged allocations, and restore the original binding only
after the last VLAN leaves. Prevent egress setup from overriding it.
Quarantine failed rollback/restore resources.

Expose port ownership and fallback readback in existing diagnostics.
Keep code-89 interval counts and one sampled descriptor per minute without
repeated suppression notices. Keep source checks and dual-tag support.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
